<% title "Electronic delivery of tax forms" %>

<% form_type = @legal_entity.latest_completed_tax_form.form_type == "W9" ? "1099" : "1042-S" %>

<h1>Electronic delivery of tax forms</h1>

<p>
  Thanks for submitting your tax form for <%= @legal_entity.name %>. If <%= @legal_entity.person? ? "you receive" : "#{@legal_entity.name} receives" %>
  payments through HCB that must be reported to the IRS, Hack Club will furnish
  <%= @legal_entity.person? ? "you" : "it" %> a Form <%= form_type %> after the end of the year.
  You can choose to receive these forms electronically instead of on paper.
</p>

<div class="card mb3">
  <h2 class="mt0">Your choice</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>
      You don't have to consent to electronic delivery. If you don't consent, we'll mail you a paper copy of
      each Form <%= form_type %> to the address on your tax form.
    </strong>
  </p>

  <h2>What you're consenting to</h2>
  <p>
    Your consent applies to every Form <%= form_type %> that Hack Club furnishes to <%= @legal_entity.name %>, for the current tax year
    and every future tax year, until you withdraw it.
  </p>

  <h2>How you'll receive your forms</h2>
  <p>
    By the IRS due date (generally January 31, or February 15 for some forms), we'll post your form on HCB and email
    <%= @legal_entity.emails.to_sentence %> to let you know it's available, with instructions on how to view and print it.
    Each form will remain available on HCB through at least October 15 of the year it's furnished, so be sure to print or
    save a copy for your records.
  </p>

  <h2>Hardware and software requirements</h2>
  <p>To access your forms, you'll need:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A computer or mobile device with an internet connection</li>
    <li>A current version of a web browser, such as Chrome, Firefox, Safari, or Edge</li>
    <li>Access to your HCB account</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If these requirements change in a way that could affect your ability to access your forms, we'll notify you before
    furnishing your next form and ask you to consent again.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting a paper copy</h2>
  <p>
    Even after you consent, you can request a paper copy of any Form <%= form_type %> at no cost by emailing
    <%= mail_to "hcb@hackclub.com" %>. Requesting a paper copy doesn't withdraw your consent unless you tell us it should.
  </p>

  <h2>Withdrawing your consent</h2>
  <p>
    You can withdraw your consent at any time by notifying us in writing, either by emailing <%= mail_to "hcb@hackclub.com" %>
    or by mail to Hack Club, 8605 Santa Monica Boulevard #86294, West Hollywood, CA 90069. We'll confirm your withdrawal
    in writing (by email or mail). Withdrawing your consent applies to forms we haven't yet furnished; it doesn't
    affect forms that have already been furnished to you electronically.
  </p>

  <h2>When electronic delivery ends</h2>
  <p>
    We'll stop furnishing your forms electronically, and send them on paper instead, if you withdraw your consent, if
    your HCB account is closed, if our emails to you can't be delivered, or if HCB stops offering electronic delivery.
    We'll let you know in writing if we stop furnishing your forms electronically.
  </p>

  <h2>Keeping your information up to date</h2>
  <p>
    <% if @legal_entity.managed? %>
      Your email address is managed by <%= @legal_entity.managing_event.name %>; contact them to update it.
    <% else %>
      You can update your email address in your <%= link_to "account settings", my_settings_path %>.
    <% end %>
    To update your name, address, or taxpayer identification number, submit a new tax form from your
    <%= link_to "payment information page", legal_entity_path(@legal_entity) %>. You can also contact us at
    <%= mail_to "hcb@hackclub.com" %> for help.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="card mb3">
  <%= form_with url: electronic_consent_tax_form_path(@form), method: :post do |form| %>
    <%= form.hidden_field :electronic_consent, value: "true" %>

    <div class="field field--checkbox">
      <%= form.check_box :consent_acknowledgement, { required: true }, "true", nil %>
      <%= form.label :consent_acknowledgement do %>
        I have read the information above and consent to receive Forms <%= form_type %> for <%= @legal_entity.name %> electronically.
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="flex justify-between">
      <%= form.submit "Consent to electronic delivery", class: "btn bg-success" %>
      <%= button_to "No thanks, mail me paper copies", electronic_consent_tax_form_path(@form), params: { electronic_consent: "false" }, class: "btn bg-muted" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
